# Development-mode defaults (TRACKED — safe: no hostnames, no secrets).
# Vite loads this file for `npm run dev` with HIGHER priority than
# frontend/.env, so local development ALWAYS calls relative `/api/...`,
# which the Vite dev proxy forwards to the local backend
# (http://localhost:3001) — even if a frontend/.env file containing a
# production URL exists. Production builds never read this file; they use
# frontend/.env.* production files or, on Vercel, the real
# VITE_API_BASE_URL environment variable.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
